<section class="warning">
<h2>IMPORTANT: Veterinary care comes first</h2>
<p>This resource provides educational first-aid information only. It does not replace veterinary diagnosis, treatment or professional advice.</p>
<p>If an animal is struggling to breathe, unconscious, collapsing, bleeding severely, having repeated seizures or experiencing another life-threatening emergency, contact an emergency veterinarian immediately.</p>
<p>Do not delay transport or professional care to complete this guide. If veterinary services are far away, telephone the nearest veterinary hospital for instructions while arranging transport.</p>
</section>

